---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ImageSlot from '../components/ImageSlot.astro';
import Todo from '../components/Todo.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Kennedy Campbell, UX designer, skateboarder, and creator.">
  <div class="container about">
    <h1 class="page-title bleed-red">About</h1>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="photo">
        <ImageSlot
          folder="about"
          name="portrait"
          alt="Kennedy Campbell smiling against a red wall, wearing glasses and a black fur trapper hat"
          hint="A portrait of you. Square or 4:5 works best."
          ratio="4 / 5"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="text">
        <!-- Her own words, from her Framer draft. Light edits only. -->
        <p class="lead">
          Thanks for stopping by! I'm Kennedy, a UX designer originally from West Bloomfield, Michigan. I'm passionate
          about creating intuitive experiences that solve real problems.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Walmart Global Tech, I design the UI for ReimburseMe, Walmart's expense reimbursement app. I studied
          Experience Architecture (human-computer interaction) at Michigan State University, and I designed Ani, an
          animanga social app.
        </p>
        <p>Outside of design, I'm a sponsored skateboarder and creator who loves exploring new ways to stay creative.</p>
        <Todo label="Kennedy: music">
          Nacho mentioned you produce music, and the home page now lists "music production" under Off the clock. Is that right? If so, add
          one line here about what you make, and a link if you want people to listen.
        </Todo>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          I believe great design goes beyond aesthetics. It's about understanding people. I focus on identifying user
          needs, simplifying complex interactions, and designing solutions that feel natural and intuitive.
        </p>
        <p>
          And I love visual QA. Comparing what shipped against the design and chasing down every mismatch is like
          solving a puzzle.
        </p>

        <!-- Experience, education, and skills moved from her old portfolio on 2026-11-05, rewritten at her level. -->
        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <ol class="timeline">
          <li>
            <p class="mono when">Jul 2025 – now</p>
            <h3>UX Designer · Walmart Global Tech</h3>
            <p class="mono muted where">Bentonville, AR</p>
            <p>I design UI for flows in ReimburseMe, Walmart's expense app, on a team led by a senior UX designer.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="mono when">Jun – Aug 2024</p>
            <h3>Product Management Specialist Intern · Walmart Global Tech</h3>
            <p class="mono muted where">Bentonville, AR</p>
            <p>Prioritized roadmaps, ran competitive analysis, prototyped an internal expense platform, and presented to the CTO.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="mono when">Jun 2024</p>
            <h3>Web Design Intern · MSU ADA Accessibility</h3>
            <p class="mono muted where">West Bloomfield, MI</p>
            <p>Made wireframes and prototypes and ran usability tests to shape a client's accessibility roadmap.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="mono when">Feb 2022 – Jun 2025</p>
            <h3>UX Design Lead · Ani</h3>
            <p class="mono muted where">Nashville, TN</p>
            <p>Designed the core experience and design system for an animanga social app. The MVP reached 10K+ downloads in its first month.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Education</h2>
        <p><strong>B.A. Experience Architecture (human-computer interaction)</strong><br />
          <span class="mono muted">Michigan State University · May 2025</span></p>

        <h2>Skills and tools</h2>
        <p class="mono muted label">Practice</p>
        <ul class="tags">
          {['User research', 'Usability testing', 'Wireframing', 'Prototyping', 'Information architecture', 'User flows', 'Visual QA', 'Agile / Scrum', 'Product lifecycle management', 'B2B and B2C'].map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="mono muted label">Tools</p>
        <ul class="tags">
          {['Figma', 'Figma Make', 'Adobe Creative Suite', 'Miro', 'Jira', 'Confluence', 'Canva', 'HTML / CSS', 'VS Code', 'GitHub'].map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <!-- From her Wix site's "Skate Sponsorship (2021 – current)" tile, 2026-11-05. Kept small on purpose. -->
        <h2>Skateboarding</h2>
        <p>I've been a sponsored skateboarder since 2021.</p>
        <ImageSlot
          folder="about"
          name="skate"
          alt="Kennedy skateboarding"
          hint="A photo or video still of you skating"
          ratio="4 / 3"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: 3rem; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); align-items: start; }
  .photo :global(.slot) { margin-top: 0; }
  .photo :global(img) { border: var(--rule); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .lead { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .text h2 { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1rem 0 0; border-top: var(--rule); }
  .timeline li { padding: 1.25rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .timeline h3 { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .timeline p { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; }
  .when { margin: 0 !important; }
  .label { margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .tags { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .tags li { border: 1px solid currentColor; padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
